Description: TuxWall Network Firewall Dashboard
 Modern web dashboard for a home/edge router featuring DHCP lease management,
 Unbound DNS and blocklist control, UFW firewall rules, WireGuard VPN status,
 CrowdSec integration, live attack map with animated arcs, bandwidth charts,
 AI Assistant (Claude/Ollama/OpenAI) with live system context and one-click
 rule changes, themed UI with glassmorphism effects, and dark/light themes.
 .
 v2.2.0 adds: DHCP static IP reservation management (add/edit/delete via
 kea-dhcp4.conf with live Kea reload, click-to-fill from leases table),
 fetchJSON options fix (POST body was silently dropped causing 404 on all
 VLAN/PF/DMZ actions), CrowdSec main window overflow fix, scrollbar theming,
 mobile layout fix for full-width main panel.
 .
 v2.3.0 adds: embedded opencode AI agent with interactive permission
 prompts, OPNsense-style User Manager (add/edit/disable users, per-user
 admin rights), and TOTP two-factor authentication (QR-code enrollment
 with Google Authenticator/Aegis/1Password, per-step replay protection).
 .
 v2.4.0 adds: firewall restore baseline (save/restore live rulesets, atomic
 iptables-restore with verification) replacing the destructive flush-all reset;
 system backup overhaul — include/exclude config checklist, browse archive
 contents, per-file download and single-file restore with .bak snapshots and
 service-restart hints, sanitized exports for safe sharing (WireGuard/CrowdSec/
 cloudflared/tuxwall secrets dropped or redacted), upload-and-examine restore
 flow, auto-prune retention, root-only archive permissions, and dashboard files
  now captured in the system backup.
  .
  v2.5.0 adds: unified glassmorphism button system matching the sidebar nav —
  accent-tinted translucent gradients with backdrop blur, glowing borders and
  hover glow on all buttons (primary, ghost, danger, segmented tabs, service
  tabs, login, icon buttons and file-selector buttons), light-theme contrast
  overrides, and cache-bust bump.
  .
  v2.5.1 adds: attack map tile fix — CARTO now watermarks keyless raster
  basemaps; tiles now carry a registered CARTO key (?key= param, the
  documented parameter name), plus cache-bust bump.
  Served by nginx from /var/www/html, backed by a Python API server running
 as the systemd unit tuxwall.service on port 8008.

